{
  "name": "AI Shipment Support Bot - Skeleton",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Ingest, two channels into one shape\nAll-Inkl email over IMAP and Amazon Message Center over the Selling Partner API are normalized into a single internal message: sender, body, channel, thread id, locale. The rest of the flow does not care where the message came from.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 620
      },
      "id": "sticky-ingest",
      "name": "Lane 1 Ingest",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-imap",
      "name": "All-Inkl IMAP Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailReadImap",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [40, 60]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-amazon-poll",
      "name": "Amazon Messaging Poll",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [40, 160]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-normalize",
      "name": "Normalize Message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [340, 110]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Understand\nOne small-model call extracts the order reference, customer hints, and an intent label from a fixed set: shipment status, tracking correction, out of scope. Every field comes back with a confidence score. The router branches on the label.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 620
      },
      "id": "sticky-understand",
      "name": "Lane 2 Understand",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, 360]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-extract",
      "name": "Extract Order + Intent (small LLM)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [40, 420]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-router",
      "name": "Intent Router",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [340, 420]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Ground in your data\nDeterministic call to the ERP interface with the order reference. Returns tracking link, number, carrier, status. No model involved. The guard handles not found, multiple matches, and a slow or failing ERP: retry, then hand off.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 620
      },
      "id": "sticky-ground",
      "name": "Lane 3 Ground",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, 680]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-erp",
      "name": "ERP Tracking Lookup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [40, 740]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-guard",
      "name": "Guard: No Match / ERP Down",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [340, 740]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Reply\nA German template carries the structure and the formal Sie tone. The model only adjusts wording for the case. Tracking facts from lane 3 are inserted verbatim and never passed through the model as free text. The gate decides auto-send vs human draft and runs the Amazon policy filter.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 620
      },
      "id": "sticky-reply",
      "name": "Lane 4 Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, 1000]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-compose",
      "name": "Compose German Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [40, 1060]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-gate",
      "name": "Confidence + Amazon Policy Gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [340, 1060]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Outbound and record\nReply goes out on the original channel (SMTP reply or Amazon message). Anything low-confidence, unmatched, or out of scope goes to the human queue with full context. Every decision and every ERP field used is written to the audit log.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 620
      },
      "id": "sticky-out",
      "name": "Lane 5 Out",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, 1320]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-send",
      "name": "Send Reply (origin channel)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailSend",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [40, 1380]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-handoff",
      "name": "Human Handoff Queue",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [340, 1380]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-audit",
      "name": "Audit Log",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [40, 1480]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "All-Inkl IMAP Trigger": {
      "main": [[{ "node": "Normalize Message", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]]
